0009: the framebuffer console is the serial device when the ADT names none (xnu-12377 serial_init).

12377's serial_init() returns 0 when /chosen has no serial-device phandle, before setting serial_do_transmit or
calling the registered devices' init. The 7T has no UART, only our fbcon (0003, registered by fbcon_probe() just
before), so every kernel printf was dropped after early boot: boots 27d/27e showed nothing after EARLY 20 (USB
network up, ping answered), and the console ring behind the UDP live log (0077) stayed empty.

diff --git a/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c b/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
index d63130e..09c55c6 100644
--- a/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
+++ b/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
@@ -1061,6 +1061,21 @@ serial_init(void)
 	// Get the phandle of the serial device XNU has been configured to use.
 	uint32_t phandle;
 	if (!get_serial_device_phandle(&phandle)) {
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+		/*
+		 * SWEET: no serial-device phandle, but the framebuffer console is registered. Without this, 12377
+		 * returned 0 here: serial_do_transmit stayed 0, fbcon was never init'ed and every printf/kprintf was
+		 * dropped (boots 27d/27e: nothing on screen after EARLY 20, empty console ring, no UDP live log).
+		 */
+		if (gPESF != NULL) {
+			for (fns = gPESF; fns != NULL; fns = fns->next) {
+				serial_do_transmit = 1;
+				fns->init();
+			}
+			uart_initted = true;
+			return 1;
+		}
+#endif
 		// XNU has not been configured to use a serial device; return early.
 		return 0;
 	}
